<article class="env-lemma" id="02C8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02C8">Lemma <span data-tag="02C8">10.9.13</span>.</a> Localization respects quotients, i.e. if $N$ is a submodule of $M$, then $S^{-1}(M/N)\simeq (S^{-1}M)/(S^{-1}N)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      From the exact sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \longrightarrow N \longrightarrow M \longrightarrow M/N \longrightarrow 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  0 \longrightarrow S^{-1}N \longrightarrow S^{-1}M \longrightarrow S^{-1}(M/N) \longrightarrow 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       The corollary then follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>